<article class="env-lemma" id="83E5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/83E5">Lemma <span data-tag="83E5">6.5.2.9</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos, and let $n < \infty $. Then $\tau _{\leq n} \calX \subseteq \calX ^{\wedge }$. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Corollary <a href="/tag/D829" data-tag="D829">6.5.1.14</a> implies that an $n$-truncated object of $\calX $ is local with respect to every $n$-connective morphism of $\calX $, and therefore with respect to every $\infty $-connective morphism of $\calX $. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>